# Explore RAG

```elixir
Mix.install(
  [
    {:bumblebee, "~> 0.6.3"},
    {:exla, ">= 0.0.0"}
  ],
  config: [nx: [default_backend: EXLA.Backend]]
)
```

## References

* [Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) with Elixir](https://shapath.com.np/posts/beginning-rag-elixir/)
* [A RAG for Elixir in Elixir](https://bitcrowd.dev/a-rag-for-elixir-in-elixir/)
* [A RAG Library for Elixir](https://bitcrowd.dev/a-rag-library-for-elixir/?utm_source=elixir-merge)
* [How to use Jina embeddings in Elixir with Bumblebee](https://bitcrowd.dev/how-to-run-jina-embeddings-in-elixir/)
* [Notes on semantic search with Elixir and Bumblebee](https://dev.to/ndrean/an-example-of-semantic-search-with-elixir-and-bumblebee-h9n)
* [Bumblebee -- LLMs and RAG](https://hexdocs.pm/bumblebee/llms_rag.html)
* [Elixir Machine Learning: Clustering, Bumblebee, and Structured Prompting](https://dockyard.com/blog/2024/03/05/elixir-machine-learning-clustering-bumblebee-structured-prompting)
* [Generate embeddings with nomic-embed-text-v1 using Elixir Bumblebee](https://natetodd.com/blog/generate-embeddings-with-nomic-embed-text-v1-using-elixir-bumblebee)

## General Steps

* Document Ingestion (Input)
* Chunking
* Embedding & Vector Database
* Generation & Output

## Models I need from Huggingface

```elixir
{:ok, model} = 
  Bumblebee.load_model({:hf, "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"})
```

```elixir
{:ok, model_info} = Bumblebee.load_model({:hf, "bert-base-uncased"}, architecture: :base)
{:ok, tokenizer} = Bumblebee.load_tokenizer({:hf, "bert-base-uncased"})

text = "Hello, world!"
inputs = Bumblebee.apply_tokenizer(tokenizer, text)

Axon.predict(model_info.model, model_info.params, inputs).hidden_state[0]
```

```elixir
repo = {:hf, "jinaai/jina-embeddings-v2-base-en"}

{:ok, model_info} = Bumblebee.load_model(repo, architecture: :base)
{:ok, tokenizer} = Bumblebee.load_tokenizer(repo)

serving =
  Bumblebee.Text.TextEmbedding.text_embedding(model_info, tokenizer,
    compile: [batch_size: 64, sequence_length: 512],
    defn_options: [compiler: EXLA],
    output_attribute: :hidden_state,
    output_pool: :mean_pooling
  )
```
